@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/referencing/{agent_id} — which teams a deletion would break
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Agent owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "Client\n(generated AIAgentsTeamsApi)" as Client #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nread node" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> Client : agentsTeamsReferencingTeams
Client -> API : GET .../{address}/referencing/{agent_id}
API -> Domain : referencing_teams(address, agent_id)
Domain -> Chain : list the wallet's teams
Chain --> Domain : team headers
loop every team, bounded concurrency
  Domain -> Chain : read the team's LATEST version
  Chain --> Domain : serializations
  Domain -> Domain : parse; does it reference the agent?
end
alt every team readable
  Domain --> API : ReferencingTeam[]\n{ id, name, version, published,\n  published_handle? }
  API --> Client : 200 (possibly empty array)
  Client --> Owner : what deletion would break
else any team unreadable
  API <-- Domain : error — a partial list would\nunder-report the breakage
  Client <-- API : 500 InternalError
end

note over Domain #FFF0C7
Latest versions only, deliberately: a team whose
newest version no longer uses the agent is not
broken going forward. The check exists because a
deleted referent leaves a team permanently
undeployable while its canvas still draws the
node by name — there is no dangling edge to see.
end note
@enduml
